---
functor: 1
title: Common errors
---

set heading(numbering: none)

Each problem has a line, a column, a message and a hint. Errors stop the output from being correct. Warnings do not. Run `functor check file.fn` to see them all.

# LaTeX habits

| You wrote | Message | Fix |
|:--|:--|:--|
| `\alpha` | the backslash shows as a sign | `alpha` |
| `\frac{a}{b}` | unknown symbol, or braces shown | `frac(a, b)` |
| `x_{i+1}` | braces shown in the script | `x_(i + 1)` |
| `dx` | "`dx` is not a symbol name, so it shows as single letters." | `d x` |
| `!=` | the two signs show as they are | `eq.not` |
| `a & b \\ c & d` | the signs show as they are | `mat(a, b; c, d)` |
| `\text{if}` | the backslash shows | `"if"` |

# Names and operations

| Message | Fix |
|:--|:--|
| "Unknown symbol `alpah`." with "Did you mean `alpha`?" | Correct the name. |
| "Unknown operation `circel`." with "Did you mean `circle`?" | Correct the operation. |
| "`bb` works only on a single capital letter." | Use one capital letter: `R.bb`. |
| "`frak` works only on a single letter, as the first operation." | Put the style operation first: `g.frak.hat`. |
| "`x` has 4 operations." (warning) | Use at most three, or define a `sym`. |
| "`(v).vbar.x2` looks the same as `norm(v)`..." (warning) | Write the meaning form. See [Notation check and trace](help/notation.html). |
| "`v` is a vector, and the style rule draws vectors with `.arrow`..." (warning) | Remove the hand style, or change the `set vec` rule. |
| "Operation `deform` is not in Functor 1." (also `stretch`) | Write `tall` or `wide`: `integral.tall`, `to.wide`. |
| "Operation `fuse` is not in Functor 1." | Use `join(a, b)` for now. |
| "`left` works only after a fence." | Write a fence first: `(x).brace.left`. |

# Brackets and calls

| Message | Fix |
|:--|:--|
| "This `(` is not closed." | Add the closing bracket. |
| "A script needs something before it." | Write the base first: `x_1`. |
| "This term has two `_` scripts." | Put both in one group: `x_(i j)`. |
| "`frac` takes 2 arguments, but it has 1." | `frac(top, bottom)`. |
| "`join` takes two single symbols." | Build each side first: `join(o.up, r.up)`. |
| "`wrap` needs single symbols as its fences." | `wrap(L.script, x + y)`. |
| "The rows of this `mat` have different numbers of cells." (warning) | Give each row the same number of cells. A cell can be empty. |

# Document

| Message | Fix |
|:--|:--|
| "This file does not state its language version." (warning) | Add `functor: 1` to the front matter. |
| "The label `eq:nope` does not exist." | Correct the label, or add it. For a plain at sign, write `\@`. |
| "The label `eq:a` is used twice." | Rename one of them. |
| "The block `theorem` is not closed." | Add a line `:::`. |
| "Unknown block `theorm`." | Correct the kind. |
| "This figure has no caption." (warning) | Add a line `Caption: ...`. |
| "`set pgae` is not known." | Correct the rule name. |
| "`nope` is not a fence." | Use a fence name, `none`, or one symbol. |
| "This math has no closing `$`." | Add `$`. For a dollar sign, write `\$`. |

# Known gaps

- `text(x)` sets its argument as math today. Use quotes for words.
- `{n}` values do not work in math yet.
- Lists do not nest yet.
- Error messages have no stable codes yet.
